# Every delivered file must land byte for byte as it was built. The SDC looks like text, and
# git duly normalised its CRLF to LF on commit -- which changed its length from 1339 to 1314
# bytes and, with it, the SHA-1 that SceneList.xml has to carry. Sony's own SDCs use CRLF, so
# these are marked binary and git keeps its hands off.
*.sdc    binary
*.SDAT   binary
*.mp4    binary
*.png    binary

# Checked out with LF whatever the platform: git was giving it CRLF on Windows, and `md5sum -c`
# then read every filename with a trailing carriage return and failed to open any of them.
CHECKSUMS.md5  text eol=lf
